<title>UK: LUKoil raises $125 mln via privately placed bond.</title>
<headline>LUKoil raises $125 mln via privately placed bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's biggest oil company NK LUKoil raised $125 million via a privately placed bond issue this week, bankers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal was issued via LUKoil's Dutch subsidiary and had a one-year maturity. It was placed with between 10 and 30 institutional investors, they said.</p>
<p>Bankers said the transaction was arranged via Credit Suisse First Boston, but officials there declined to comment.</p>
<p>In June, LUKoil said it could issue bonds backed by oil on the international capital markets this year. In 1998 it is expected to sell a 15 stake in the company.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
